  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is an Attribute?</h2>
    <p>An attribute gives extra information to a tag. For example, <b>href</b> tells where the link will go, and <b>src</b> tells where the image is located.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Structure:</b> &lt;tag attribute="value"&gt;Text&lt;/tag&gt;<br>Example: &lt;a href="https://google.com"&gt;Google&lt;/a&gt;</div>
    <h2>2. Link - &lt;a&gt; Tag</h2>
    <p>To create a clickable link on a website, we use the <b>&lt;a&gt;</b> tag. In the <b>href</b> attribute, we write the address where the user will go after clicking.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"https://www.google.com"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Go to Google</span><span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">Go to Google</a> ← Click to try it</div>
    <h2>3. Open Link in New Tab - target="_blank"</h2>
    <p>If you want the link to open in a new tab, add <b>target="_blank"</b>.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"https://www.youtube.com"</span> <span class="attr">target</span>=<span class="val">"_blank"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Open YouTube in New Tab</span><span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><a href="https://www.youtube.com" target="_blank">Open YouTube in New Tab</a></div>
    <h2>4. Image - &lt;img&gt; Tag</h2>
    <p>To add an image, we use the <b>&lt;img&gt;</b> tag. It has <b>no closing tag</b>.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="attr">src</span>=<span class="val">"my-photo.jpg"</span> <span class="attr">alt</span>=<span class="val">"My Photo"</span> <span class="attr">width</span>=<span class="val">"300"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Attribute</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>src</b></td><td>Image name or link (Source)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>alt</b></td><td>If the image does not load, this text will be shown. It is also important for Google / SEO.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>width / height</b></td><td>Size of the image</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="result">
      <p>Example Image:</p>
      <img class="demo-img" src="https://picsum.photos/300/180" alt="Demo Image">
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">This image is coming from the internet — its link is written in src.</p>
    </div>
    <h2>5. Image from Internet vs Computer</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">&lt;!-- From the Internet --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="attr">src</span>=<span class="val">"https://picsum.photos/300/200"</span> <span class="attr">alt</span>=<span class="val">"Random"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="text">&lt;!-- From Your Computer - image must be in the same folder --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="attr">src</span>=<span class="val">"cat.jpg"</span> <span class="attr">alt</span>=<span class="val">"My Cat"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Clickable Image - Link + Image Together</h2>
    <p>To open a link when someone clicks on an image, put the image inside the &lt;a&gt; tag.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"https://google.com"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="attr">src</span>=<span class="val">"logo.png"</span> <span class="attr">alt</span>=<span class="val">"Google"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Full Example</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">My Favourite Websites</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"https://google.com"</span> <span class="attr">target</span>=<span class="val">"_blank"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Google</span><span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;br&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"https://youtube.com"</span> <span class="attr">target</span>=<span class="val">"_blank"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">YouTube</span><span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="attr">src</span>=<span class="val">"my-pic.jpg"</span> <span class="attr">alt</span>=<span class="val">"My Pic"</span> <span class="attr">width</span>=<span class="val">"200"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Homework</h2>
    <p>Create a page that has: <b>2 Links</b> (Google, YouTube) and <b>1 Image</b>. Make the image clickable.</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> a = Link | href = Where to go | target="_blank" = New Tab | img = Image | src = Image address | alt = Text if image does not load</div>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
